# No AI slop defaults

Apply these unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.

## Copy and communication

- Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`). Use commas, periods, colons, or parentheses.
- Never use emojis in UI strings, Slack payloads, comments, commits, logs, or docs.
- Prefer plain, specific wording. Avoid hype, filler, and stock assistant phrasing.

## UI

- Do not add rounded corners: no new `rounded-*` Tailwind classes, no `borderRadius` / `borderTopLeftRadius` etc. in React Native StyleSheets, no pill chips.
- Exception: leave existing third-party/shadcn primitives alone unless the task is to restyle them; do not introduce extra rounding on top.
- Avoid decorative glow, purple gradients, badge clusters, and other generic AI visual defaults.

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD
<p className="rounded-xl">Welcome. We are glad you are here 🎉</p>

// GOOD
<p>Welcome. We are glad you are here.</p>
```
